      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "The equation of the ellipse centered at the origin is\n$$\\frac{x^2}{25} + \\frac{y^2}{16} = 1.$$\nTo find the foci, set $y = 0$:\n$$\\frac{x^2}{25} + 0 = 1 \\implies x^2 = 25 \\implies x = \\pm 5.$$\nSo the foci are $(\\pm 5, 0)$.\nThe circle is tangent to the ellipse, so the distance between the center of the circle and one of the foci is equal to the radius plus the distance from the center of the circle to the outside of the ellipse.\nThe distance from the center of the circle to one of the foci is the radius, so the radius of the circle is $\\boxed{2}$.\nThe answer is: 2",
